WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
On the Home screen, click Open project… and pick the project from the previous tutorial.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Click Post.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Post opens on the version Default S-H-O, the image of the previous tutorial.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Read the picture: open the zoom list and choose 100 %.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
At 100 % on the wall: the structure is soft, and the sky and the shadows are not yet deep.

6
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Fitted view: the orange of the wall and the cyan of the blue zone are still close to each other.

7
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Click New version: it duplicates the current one.

8
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Click the version name to rename the copy.

9
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.000
The copy is named Palette and finish; Default S-H-O stays as it was.

10
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Select the Starless image sub-layer: the filters added now apply to it only.

11
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Click Filter, then Color, then Colour mixer.

12
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Orange · hue: drag to about +10°.

13
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Orange · saturation: about +25 %.

14
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Red · saturation: about +15 %.

15
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Yellow · saturation: about +20 %.

16
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Aqua · saturation: about +55 %.

17
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Blue · saturation: about +35 %.

18
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Blue · hue: about −10°.

19
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:15.000
The gold of H-alpha and S II and the cyan of O III are now clearly apart.

20
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Click Filter, then Stretch, then Levels.

21
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Raise the black point a little, until the sky is deeper and the dark lanes are dark: about 0,02.

22
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Lower Gamma slightly: about 0,95.

23
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.000
Click Filter, then Contrast, then Local contrast.

24
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Raise Strength until the folds of the wall and the lanes stand out: about 0,4.

25
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Set Scale to a large radius: about 80 px.

26
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Click Filter, then Detail, then Multiscale sharpening.

27
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.000
2 px: about 0,15.

28
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.000
4 px: about 0,35.

29
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.000
8 px: about 0,5.

30
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.000
16 px: about 0,4.

31
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:54.000
The finest texture is back, and the wall starts to burn.

32
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.000
Click Filter, then Contrast, then Highlight compression.

33
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Raise Strength until the red of the wall keeps its texture: about 0,5.

34
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.000
The finished image: five filters on the starless image, in this order.

35
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Click Export.

36
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.000
Choose the JPEG format.

37
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:18.000
Check the file, on the tutorial drive, then click Export.

38
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:23.000
Save the project with Ctrl+S.
